<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices gain on plant demand.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices gain on plant demand.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices on Tuesday rose in central Indian markets on good demand from processing plants, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said prices were up by 50-100 rupees per tonne on dull. business volume and steady undertone.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices fell by 100 rupees per tonne on increased selling from plants and refineries.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were firm on limited availability against better demand. Soymeal yellow was $327-328 per tonne FAS (Free Alongside Ship) in bulk for west coast Indian ports for export. Rapeseed extraction was $130-131 per tonne FAS in bulk for export and was 4,500-4,525 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition. Business volume was dull and the undertone was steady.</p>
